  "id": "selective-response",
  "term": "selective response",
  "definition": "Selective response is a pattern in which a brain area reacts more strongly to a particular kind of visual information than to others. In the source material, it refers to ventral lateral prefrontal cortex activity that is especially responsive to faces, with the eyes appearing to contribute strongly to that response.",
